  "evidence": "The validity of a work permit can range from a few months to several years, depending on the specific country's immigration laws and the nature of the employment contract. For example, in some countries, a work permit may be issued for the duration of a specific employment contract (e.g., if you have a fixed-term contract, the permit may be valid for that period). In others, permits for permanent or long-term employment may be issued for several years (e.g., renewable every 1–2 years, or even up to five years in some cases). There is no universal one-year rule across the EU/EFTA."
